<p>Send emails from server-side JavaScript using SMTP</p>

<b>Key Features</b>
<ul><li> Send emails to single or multiple recipients</li>
<li> HTML and plain text email support</li>
<li> Configurable SMTP settings</li>
<li> Uses admin email configuration</li>
</ul>
<b>Server-Side Usage:</b>
<xmp class="panel" of-exclude="true">
// Get the Mailer API
var Mailer = js.getObject("/OpenForum/AddOn/Mailer","Mailer.sjs");

// Send email to single recipient
Mailer.sendEmail("user@example.com", "Subject", "Email content");

// Send email to multiple recipients
Mailer.sendEmail(<a href="/OpenForum/Editor?pageName=/OpenForum/AddOn/Mailer/QuickReference/"user1@example.com", "user2@example.com""target="editor" style="color: red" title="The page /OpenForum/Editor?pageName=/OpenForum/AddOn/Mailer/QuickReference/"user1@example.com", "user2@example.com" does not exist. Click to create it.">"user1@example.com", "user2@example.com"</a>, 
                 "Subject", "Email content");
</xmp>

<b>Configuration</b>
<ul><li> Admin email settings stored in `/OpenForum/Users/Admin/mailer.config`</li>
<li> Requires SMTP server configuration</li>
</ul>

<h3>Mailer Quick Reference</h3>

<b>Notes</b>
<ul><li> <a href="https://support.google.com/a/answer/176600?hl=en" target="external_page">Google SMTP Settings</a></li>
